{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789323081,"nonce":"gCkpXZIldFXb1XVrcN7l1HWxPQU=","title":"Interop call costs against each language's own calls","message":"`cargo bench -p caribou-interop` (benches/interop.rs): one operation\nlooped n times inside a function of the calling language, timed as one\ncall, median of runs, ns per iteration. Columns: Haxe→Haxe and Wren→Wren\nare the baselines, Haxe→Wren and Wren→Haxe the bridge.\n\nFirst numbers, this machine, ash hybrid + wren_lift tiered, n = 100k,\nmedian of 3, after the per-slot cache of a static's or constructor's\ntarget (registry generation) landed:\n\n    static call        6.3     49.5    373.4    359.5\n    method call        3.4     38.3    288.9    452.2\n    getter             3.4      3.6    204.8    154.5\n    setter             0.7      3.7    274.6    138.5\n    closure call       3.4     83.9    170.9    368.1\n    construct          5.9     79.2    470.1    436.6\n\nBefore the cache, Haxe→Wren static was 1122 and construct 1224: every\ncall resolved the class by name through the registry (three String\nallocations for the candidate spellings, two locks, a scan by\nsignature). ash interp + wren_lift interpreter: Haxe→Wren 347–862,\nWren→Haxe 207–557, baselines 30–140 (Haxe) and 120–180 (Wren).\n\nWhere the rest goes, by reading the paths, unmeasured:\n\nHaxe→Wren (import.rs run): dyn_to_value per argument (a Str or HaxeRef\nallocation for non-scalars); bridge::invoke → the Wren protocol's invoke\ntakes the member as a core Symbol and looks its name up in the VM's\ninterner (a string hash) in has_method and again in call_method_on's\nintern; call_closure_sync pushes a MIR frame and runs the interpreter\nloop rather than the tier's code; the result comes back through\nvalue_to_dyn with a box allocation for a number.\n\nWren→Haxe (caribou-wren import.rs dispatch): cross_in roots every\nargument with a core handle; the receiver is wrapped in a fresh HaxeRef\n(an allocation) on every call; typed dispatch boxes each argument into a\nvdynamic (allocations), arms a trap (setjmp) and goes through\nhlp_dyn_call and the closure runner; the result crosses back through\nto_wren.\n\nCandidates, in order of expected return: a Wren SymbolId cached per core\nSymbol per VM so no string is hashed per call; the receiver's HaxeRef\nkept per object (the identity gap in 0268f40 pays twice); scalars\npassed to typed Haxe natives without a vdynamic box (the dispatcher can\nplace an i32 or f64 directly for a typed signature); a direct call into\nthe Wren tier's compiled body when one exists instead of the interpreter\nloop; one trap per crossing rather than per call when calls nest.","files":null}]}